IMPORT prelude

-- Banking Act 1959 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- are my deposits protected if my bank fails, and what happens to money I
-- leave untouched: s 5(1) ("account-holder", "declared ADI") and s 5(4)-(7) ("protected account"); Part II Division 2AA, the
-- Financial Claims Scheme -- s 16AD (the Minister's declaration that switches the scheme on for one ADI, and that it cannot be
-- revoked), s 16AF (the entitlement: balance plus accrued interest, the equal shares of a joint account), s 16AG (the limit per
-- account-holder per ADI), s 16AH (how I am paid; an account opened for me without my consent), s 16AHA (the annual statement
-- within 14 days after the financial year), s 16AI (APRA takes my place as creditor to the extent of my entitlement), s 16AIC(3)
-- (entitlement reduced to nil once a transferred liabilities determination takes effect); and s 69 (unclaimed moneys: 7 years
-- untouched, the children's account exclusion, the yearly payment to the Commonwealth, and getting the money back).
--
-- SEAT: the depositor -- the account-holder of a deposit account with an ADI (in the lives, Chloe, aged seven, with a children's
-- savings account and her mother as signatory). Every exported question is phrased as that person would ask it. Division 2AA
-- speaks of what the Minister may declare and what APRA must pay; that is encoded as what I am entitled to and how I am paid.
--
-- Edition: Banking Act 1959, compilation register id C2026C00104, retrieved 13 October 2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C1959A00006.txt. The Banking Regulation 2016 is NOT deposited. It sets the s 16AG limit, the
-- s 16AF clearance adjustment, the accounts prescribed for s 5(4)(a) and 5(7), and the s 69 variations; each is an INPUT here.
-- The lives use a limit of $250,000, an input value taken from the encoding plan, not from any deposited text.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 16AE (advice to the Minister), ss 16AIA-16AIB (how APRA works out a transferred liabilities determination: only
-- its effect on me, s 16AIC(3), is encoded), Subdivision D (administration, ss 16AJ-16AO), Subdivision E (my residual claim in
-- the winding up: ss 16AQ-16AS address the liquidator; only s 16AR's same-kind account rule is noted, not encoded), Subdivision F
-- (disclosure on new accounts, s 16AT), Subdivision G (competition law exceptions); the pooled trust rule of s 16AF(3) (the
-- trustee is the single account-holder, which the joint-share rule already gives); covered financial products other than
-- accounts beyond s 5(6); everything else in the Act (authorisation, prudential supervision, statutory management, the ADI's
-- offences under s 69(3AA), (5A), (7A)), which is addressed to ADIs and APRA and sets nothing a depositor is entitled to. The
-- set-off under Corporations Act s 553C is not modelled.
--
-- Borrowed terms asked as facts: whether my bank is an ADI or a foreign ADI (s 5(1) defines them by reference to authorisation
-- under s 9, a matter of record); "net credit balance"; "children's account" is worked out from the s 69(12) facts.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to whom the law is applied, with
-- the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Banking Act 1959 -- the depositor`

§§ `Domain`

-- One account the depositor keeps with one ADI, as the depositor could describe it.
DECLARE Account HAS
    `kept with an ADI`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `bank must repay the balance on demand or at an agreed time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed by the regulations as a protected account` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed by the regulations as not protected`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `recorded in Australian currency`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a covered financial product that is not an account` IS A BOOLEAN
    `net credit balance at the declaration time`         IS A NUMBER
    `interest accrued but not credited`                  IS A NUMBER
    `clearance adjustment under the regulations`         IS A NUMBER
    `number of account-holders`                          IS A NUMBER

-- The facts about the bank and the scheme on the day the depositor asks.
DECLARE Bank HAS
    `is an ADI`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a foreign ADI`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `APRA has applied under s 16AAA for it to be wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Banking Act statutory manager is in control`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has declared it under s 16AD`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the declaration time is on or after 12 October 2011` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a declared ADI on 12 October 2011`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `a transfer certificate under a transferred liabilities determination has issued` IS A BOOLEAN

-- What the depositor gets from APRA under Subdivision C.
DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `Paid by APRA` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `Nothing: the scheme has not been switched on for my bank`
    `Nothing: I have no protected account in credit with my bank`
    `Nothing from APRA: my protected accounts went to a receiving body`

-- s 16AH(1): the ways an entitlement may be met.
DECLARE `Way of payment` IS ONE OF
    `paid to me as a single amount or in instalments`
    `applied for my benefit, for example by opening an account for me with another ADI`
    `partly paid to me and the rest applied for my benefit`

§§ `s 5(1) -- account-holder`

-- s 5(1): "account-holder means an entity ... that holds in its name, or keeps in its name, (either alone or jointly with another
-- entity) an account or covered financial product with an ADI." (Gloss: the person whose name the account is in. A signatory
-- whose name the account is not in is not, on these words, an account-holder -- an INFERENCE from "in its name".)
@export Am I an account-holder of this account (s 5(1))?
GIVEN `the account is in my name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the account is held or kept in your name, alone or jointly
      `kept with an ADI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the account is with an authorised deposit-taking institution (a bank, building society or credit union)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an account-holder` IF
    `the account is in my name` AND `kept with an ADI`

§§ `s 5(4)-(7) -- protected account`

-- s 5(4): "a protected account is an account ... kept by an account-holder ... with an ADI and either: (a) is an account that is
-- prescribed by the regulations ...; or (b) is an account ... kept under an agreement ... requiring the ADI to pay the
-- account-holder, on demand ... or at a time agreed by them, the net credit balance". s 5(5): "An account is not a protected
-- account on and after 12 October 2011 unless: (a) it is recorded in Australian currency; or (b) it is kept with an ADI that is
-- a declared ADI on 12 October 2011." s 5(6): a covered financial product that is not an account is not protected "if APRA
-- applies under section 16AAA for an order that the ADI be wound up". s 5(7): not protected if "prescribed by the regulations".
-- (Gloss: an ordinary savings, cheque or term deposit account in dollars is protected; what the regulations add or take away is
-- asked as a fact.)
@export Is my account a protected account (s 5(4)-(7))?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Account @desc Your account
      `b` IS A Bank @desc Your bank and the state of the scheme
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my account protected` IF
        `a`'s `kept with an ADI`
    AND (    `a`'s `prescribed by the regulations as a protected account`
          OR `a`'s `bank must repay the balance on demand or at an agreed time`)
    AND (    (NOT `b`'s `the declaration time is on or after 12 October 2011`)
          OR `a`'s `recorded in Australian currency`
          OR `b`'s `was a declared ADI on 12 October 2011`)
    AND (NOT (`a`'s `is a covered financial product that is not an account` AND `b`'s `APRA has applied under s 16AAA for it to be wound up`))
    AND (NOT `a`'s `prescribed by the regulations as not protected`)

§§ `s 16AD -- when the scheme is switched on`

-- s 16AD(1): "The Minister may declare that Subdivision C applies in relation to a specified ADI if any of the following
-- requirements are satisfied: (a) APRA has applied under section 16AAA for the ADI to be wound up; (b) a Banking Act statutory
-- manager is in control of the ADI's business." Note: "The Minister cannot make a declaration ... in relation to a foreign ADI
-- (see section 11E)." (Gloss: the scheme is not automatic. It is switched on, bank by bank, by the Minister, and only once the
-- bank is failing in one of these two ways. Whether the Minister does so is the Minister's choice -- asked as a fact below.)
@export Can the Government switch on the Financial Claims Scheme for my bank (s 16AD(1))?
GIVEN `b` IS A Bank @desc Your bank and the state of the scheme
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the scheme be switched on for my bank` IF
        `b`'s `is an ADI`
    AND (NOT `b`'s `is a foreign ADI`)
    AND (    `b`'s `APRA has applied under s 16AAA for it to be wound up`
          OR `b`'s `a Banking Act statutory manager is in control`)

-- s 5(1): "declared ADI means an ADI specified in a declaration under section 16AD". (Gloss: a declaration the Minister had no
-- power to make is not counted.)
@export Has the Financial Claims Scheme been switched on for my bank (s 5(1) "declared ADI")?
GIVEN `b` IS A Bank @desc Your bank and the state of the scheme
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my bank a declared ADI` IF
    `Can the scheme be switched on for my bank` `b` AND `b`'s `the Minister has declared it under s 16AD`

-- s 16AD(5): "The Minister cannot revoke a declaration made under subsection (1)."
@export Once the scheme is switched on for my bank, can it be switched off again (s 16AD(5))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the declaration be revoked` IF FALSE

§§ `s 16AF -- what I am entitled to for each account`

-- s 16AF(1): "An account-holder who has a protected account with a net credit balance with a declared ADI at the declaration
-- time is entitled to be paid by APRA an amount equal to the sum of: (a) that balance; and (b) the interest (if any) accrued by,
-- but not credited to, the account-holder ... before the declaration time; increased or decreased in accordance with the
-- regulations to take account of clearance ... of transactions". s 16AF(2): if the account "is held jointly by 2 or more
-- account-holders ..., that subsection entitles each of the account-holders to an equal share of the amount".
@export Is this account one the scheme pays me for (s 16AF(1))?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Account @desc Your account
      `b` IS A Bank @desc Your bank and the state of the scheme
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this account carry an entitlement` IF
        `Is my bank a declared ADI` `b`
    AND `Is my account protected` `a` `b`
    AND `a`'s `net credit balance at the declaration time` GREATER THAN 0

@export How much of this account is mine to claim, before the limit (s 16AF(1)-(2))?
GIVEN `a` IS AN Account @desc Your account
      `b` IS A Bank @desc Your bank and the state of the scheme
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `My share of this account before the limit` IS
    IF `Does this account carry an entitlement` `a` `b`
    THEN (  `a`'s `net credit balance at the declaration time`
          PLUS `a`'s `interest accrued but not credited`
          PLUS `a`'s `clearance adjustment under the regulations`)
         DIVIDED BY (max 1 (`a`'s `number of account-holders`))
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 16AG -- the limit`

-- s 16AG(1): "an account-holder is not entitled ... to be paid, in connection with the protected account or protected accounts
-- the account-holder has with a particular declared ADI at a particular time, one or more amounts totalling more than the limit
-- prescribed by, or worked out under, the regulations." (Gloss: one cap per person per bank, across all their accounts there,
-- their share of joint accounts included. The cap is in the Banking Regulation 2016, not deposited, so it is an INPUT.)
@export What is the most the scheme will pay me for all my accounts at this bank (s 16AG(1))?
GIVEN `the limit set by the regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc The limit per account-holder per ADI in the Banking Regulation 2016 (not deposited; enter it)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be paid at this bank` IS `the limit set by the regulations`

§§ `ss 16AF, 16AG, 16AIC -- what APRA pays me`

-- s 16AIC(3): once a certificate of transfer under a transferred liabilities determination has issued, "An account-holder's
-- entitlement under this Subdivision to be paid an amount in respect of a protected account kept with the declared ADI is reduced
-- to nil." (Gloss: the accounts move to a receiving body instead of being paid out by APRA.)
@export How much does APRA pay me if my bank fails (ss 16AF, 16AG, 16AIC)?
GIVEN `my accounts` IS A LIST OF Account @desc Every account you keep with this one bank
      `b` IS A Bank @desc Your bank and the state of the scheme
      `the limit set by the regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc The limit per account-holder per ADI (not deposited; enter it)
GIVETH AN Outcome
DECIDE `How much does APRA pay me` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`Is my bank a declared ADI` `b`))
            THEN `Nothing: the scheme has not been switched on for my bank`
        IF (NOT (any (GIVEN `a` YIELD `Does this account carry an entitlement` `a` `b`) `my accounts`))
            THEN `Nothing: I have no protected account in credit with my bank`
        IF `b`'s `a transfer certificate under a transferred liabilities determination has issued`
            THEN `Nothing from APRA: my protected accounts went to a receiving body`
        OTHERWISE `Paid by APRA` (min (`total before the limit`) (`What is the most I can be paid at this bank` `the limit set by the regulations`))
    WHERE
        `total before the limit` MEANS
            sum (map (GIVEN `a` YIELD `My share of this account before the limit` `a` `b`) `my accounts`)

@export Is all the money I hold in this bank's protected accounts covered (ss 16AF, 16AG)?
GIVEN `my accounts` IS A LIST OF Account @desc Every account you keep with this one bank
      `b` IS A Bank @desc Your bank and the state of the scheme
      `the limit set by the regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc The limit per account-holder per ADI (not deposited; enter it)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is all my protected money covered` IF
    sum (map (GIVEN `a` YIELD `My share of this account before the limit` `a` `b`) `my accounts`)
        AT MOST `the limit set by the regulations`

§§ `s 16AI -- what is left of my claim against the bank`

-- s 16AI(1): when the ADI becomes a declared ADI, my right to be paid by the ADI "(a) is reduced to the extent of the
-- account-holder's entitlement under this Subdivision ...; and (b) to the extent of the reduction, becomes a right of APRA."
-- (Gloss: for whatever the scheme pays me, APRA stands in my shoes against the bank; anything above the limit I still claim
-- myself, in the winding up. Worked out here across all my protected accounts at the bank together, since s 16AG(3) leaves the
-- split between accounts to APRA's determination. Set-off under Corporations Act s 553C is not modelled.)
@export How much can I still claim from my failed bank myself, after the scheme pays (s 16AI)?
GIVEN `my accounts` IS A LIST OF Account @desc Every account you keep with this one bank
      `b` IS A Bank @desc Your bank and the state of the scheme
      `the limit set by the regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc The limit per account-holder per ADI (not deposited; enter it)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much can I still claim from the bank` IS
    max 0 (`owed` MINUS `paid`)
    WHERE
        `owed` MEANS sum (map (GIVEN `a` YIELD `My share of this account before the limit` `a` `b`) `my accounts`)
        `paid` MEANS
            CONSIDER `How much does APRA pay me` `my accounts` `b` `the limit set by the regulations`
            WHEN `Paid by APRA` `n` THEN `n`
            OTHERWISE 0

§§ `s 16AH -- how I am paid`

-- s 16AH(1): the entitlement "may be met: (a) by paying the amount to the account-holder as a single amount or in instalments
-- ...; or (b) by applying the amount ... for the account-holder's benefit, by establishing an account with an ADI on behalf of
-- the account-holder or in another way; or (c) by paying part ... and applying the rest". (Gloss: APRA chooses; I may be given
-- money, or a new account at another bank.)
@export In what ways may APRA pay me what the scheme owes me (s 16AH(1))?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Way of payment`
DECIDE `How may I be paid` IS
    LIST `paid to me as a single amount or in instalments`,
         `applied for my benefit, for example by opening an account for me with another ADI`,
         `partly paid to me and the rest applied for my benefit`

-- s 16AH(3)-(4): APRA "may establish, on behalf of an account-holder ..., an account with an ADI (except a declared ADI)", and
-- this has effect "(a) whether or not the account-holder consents".
@export Can APRA open an account in my name at another bank without asking me (s 16AH(3)-(4))?
GIVEN `the new bank is itself a declared ADI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the bank APRA would use has itself been declared under s 16AD
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can APRA open an account for me without my consent` IF
    (NOT `the new bank is itself a declared ADI`)

-- s 16AH(5): "If an account-holder has an entitlement ... connected with a protected account of a kind prescribed by the
-- regulations for the purposes of this subsection, APRA must establish an account of the same kind on behalf of the
-- account-holder". (Gloss: which kinds are prescribed is in the regulations, not deposited -- asked as a fact.)
@export Must APRA give me a new account of the same kind as the one I lost (s 16AH(5))?
GIVEN `I have an entitlement for the account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the scheme pays you for this account
      `the account is of a kind prescribed for s 16AH(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations prescribe this kind of account for s 16AH(5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must APRA open an account of the same kind for me` IF
    `I have an entitlement for the account` AND `the account is of a kind prescribed for s 16AH(5)`

-- s 16AHA(2): "Within 14 days after the end of the financial year, APRA must give each of those account-holders a statement
-- about the amounts paid". (Gloss: the Australian financial year ends on 30 June, so the statement is due by 14 July -- the
-- 30 June end is borrowed, not stated in this Act.)
@export By how many days after the end of the financial year in which I was paid must APRA send me a statement (s 16AHA(2))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Days after year end for my statement` IS 14

@export Must APRA send me a statement for this financial year (s 16AHA(1)-(2))?
GIVEN `amount paid or applied for me in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What the scheme paid you, or applied for your benefit, in the financial year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must APRA send me a statement` IF
    `amount paid or applied for me in the year` GREATER THAN 0

§§ `s 69 -- unclaimed moneys`

-- s 69(12): "children's account means an account: (a) whose terms and conditions require it to be held by, or for the benefit
-- of, a person under 18; and (b) that is opened: (i) in the name of a person who is under 18 at the time; or (ii) by the trustee
-- of a trust for the benefit of a person who is under 18 at the time."
@export Is my account a children's account (s 69(12))?
GIVEN `terms require it to be held by or for a person under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the account's terms and conditions require it to be held by, or for the benefit of, someone under 18
      `opened in the name of a person then under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was opened in the name of someone who was under 18 at the time
      `opened by a trustee for a person then under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was opened by the trustee of a trust for someone under 18 at the time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my account a children's account` IF
        `terms require it to be held by or for a person under 18`
    AND (`opened in the name of a person then under 18` OR `opened by a trustee for a person then under 18`)

-- s 69(1): "unclaimed moneys means all ... sums of money legally payable by an ADI but in respect of which the time within which
-- proceedings may be taken for the recovery thereof has expired, and includes moneys to the credit of an account that has not
-- been operated on either by deposit or withdrawal for a period of not less than: (a) 7 years; or (b) if a greater number of years
-- is specified in the regulations -- that greater number of years". s 69(2): "the debiting of a fee ... shall be deemed not to be
-- a withdrawal and the crediting ... of interest ... shall be deemed not to be a deposit." s 69(1A): "the following are not
-- unclaimed moneys: (a) money in an account that is denominated in a currency other than Australian currency; (b) money in a
-- children's account; (c) farm management deposits". s 69(1B)-(1E): accounts and deposits specified in the regulations are
-- in or out on the regulations' conditions (asked as facts).
@export How many years untouched before money in an account becomes unclaimed (s 69(1))?
GIVEN `greater number of years specified in the regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc A greater period set by the regulations, if any (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Years untouched before money is unclaimed` IS
    max 7 `greater number of years specified in the regulations`

@export Is the money in my account unclaimed moneys (s 69(1)-(2))?
GIVEN `years since my last deposit or withdrawal` IS A NUMBER @desc Whole years since you last put money in or took money out (fees charged and interest credited do not count)
      `greater number of years specified in the regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc A greater period set by the regulations, if any (0 if none)
      `time to sue for it has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the time to take proceedings to recover the money from the bank has run out
      `is a children's account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the account is a children's account (s 69(12))
      `denominated in a foreign currency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the account is in a currency other than Australian dollars
      `is a farm management deposit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money is a farm management deposit
      `the regulations take the account out of s 69(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations specify the account or deposit as one s 69(1) does not apply to, or as unclaimed only on conditions not met (s 69(1B)-(1E))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my money unclaimed` IF
        (    `time to sue for it has expired`
          OR `years since my last deposit or withdrawal` AT LEAST `Years untouched before money is unclaimed` `greater number of years specified in the regulations`)
    AND (NOT `is a children's account`)
    AND (NOT `denominated in a foreign currency`)
    AND (NOT `is a farm management deposit`)
    AND (NOT `the regulations take the account out of s 69(1)`)

-- s 69(3): the ADI must, "within 3 months after the 31 December in each year, deliver to the Treasurer a statement ... of all
-- sums of unclaimed moneys of not less than $100 (or such other amount as is prescribed) as at the end of the year, other than
-- unclaimed moneys: (a) held in RSAs ...; (c) held in accounts ... that are operated on ... between the end of the year and the
-- day the statement is delivered ...; or (d) held in an account ... in respect of which the holder ... has notified the ADI,
-- between the end of the year and the day the statement is delivered ..., that the holder wishes to treat the account as
-- active." s 69(5): the ADI "must, at the time of the delivery of the statement, pay the Commonwealth" that total. (Gloss: what
-- this means for me -- my money goes to the Commonwealth by the end of March after the year, unless I use the account or tell
-- the bank to treat it as active in the meantime.)
@export Will my bank hand my money over to the Commonwealth (s 69(3), (5))?
GIVEN `my money is unclaimed at 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money was unclaimed moneys at the end of the calendar year
      `amount` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is in the account
      `threshold amount prescribed` IS A NUMBER @desc The reporting threshold: $100 unless another amount is prescribed
      `held in an RSA` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is held in a retirement savings account
      `I used the account after 31 December` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you deposited or withdrew before the bank sent its statement
      `I told the bank to treat it as active` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you told the bank, before it sent its statement, that you want the account treated as active
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my money go to the Commonwealth` IF
        `my money is unclaimed at 31 December`
    AND `amount` AT LEAST `threshold amount prescribed`
    AND (NOT `held in an RSA`)
    AND (NOT `I used the account after 31 December`)
    AND (NOT `I told the bank to treat it as active`)

@export By how many months after 31 December must my bank pay my unclaimed money to the Commonwealth (s 69(3), (5))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Months after 31 December for the handover` IS 3

-- s 69(7): where unclaimed moneys have been paid to the Commonwealth "and the Treasurer or an authorized officer is satisfied
-- that, but for subsection (6), a person would be paid those unclaimed moneys by the ADI ..., those unclaimed moneys shall be paid
-- to that ADI and the ADI shall thereupon pay those moneys to that person." s 69(7AA): if paid on or after 1 July 2013, "the
-- Commonwealth must also pay to the ADI the amount of interest (if any) worked out in accordance with the regulations; and (b)
-- the ADI must pay that amount to the person." (Gloss: the money is never lost; I get it back, with interest set by regulations
-- not deposited, if the Treasury is satisfied it is mine.)
@export How much do I get back of my money the Commonwealth holds (s 69(7), (7AA))?
GIVEN `amount paid to the Commonwealth` IS A NUMBER @desc The unclaimed money your bank paid to the Commonwealth
      `the Treasurer is satisfied the bank would pay me but for s 69(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Treasurer or an authorised officer is satisfied that, but for the handover, the bank would pay you
      `repaid on or after 1 July 2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the money is repaid on or after 1 July 2013
      `interest worked out under the regulations` IS A NUMBER @desc Interest under the regulations (not deposited; enter it)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much do I get back` IS
    IF `the Treasurer is satisfied the bank would pay me but for s 69(6)`
    THEN `amount paid to the Commonwealth`
         PLUS (IF `repaid on or after 1 July 2013` THEN `interest worked out under the regulations` ELSE 0)
    ELSE 0
